            <div xml:id="d844">

                <pb facs="0693" n="685" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg685"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5034 (China) Eastern Publishing Co./24:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-05-13T13:00:00-04:00">May 13, 1937—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>121. Reference your despatch No. 665, March 12,<anchor n="29" xml:id="d844-f1"/>
                    and previous correspondence in regard to the Eastern Publishing Company.
                    Inasmuch as this case seems to be substantially on all fours with the case of
                    the Searchlight Publishing Company (see correspondence between the Department
                    and the Consulate General in regard to that case, particularly Department’s
                    telegrams No. 230, July 30, 2 p.m., and No. 247, September 8, 6 p.m.,
                        1932<anchor n="30" xml:id="d844-f2"/>), the Department would appreciate
                    receiving from the Consulate General an explanatory statement of the grounds
                    upon which the Consulate General has declined to intercede on behalf of the
                    Eastern Publishing Company in an endeavor to obtain the return to the company of
                    the copies and volumes of the <hi rendition="#italic">Voice of China</hi> seized
                    by the Chinese postal authorities.</p>
                <p>Please reply by naval radio.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
